---
const features = [
  {
    title: "Import your design",
    body: "Bring SVG and DXF drawings or STL models from Inkscape, Illustrator, Fusion, FreeCAD or any CAD tool. You design elsewhere, Furrow turns it into toolpaths.",
  },
  {
    title: "The operations you need",
    body: "Profiles inside, outside or on the line with depth passes, ramp entry and holding tabs. Pockets with offset, linear or peel clearing. Drilling, engraving and V-carving.",
  },
  {
    title: "3D reliefs from STL",
    body: "Rough an STL model level by level, then finish it with parallel passes. Stack several operations on the same model: with rest machining, each one only cuts where material is left.",
  },
  {
    title: "Zero where you zero",
    body: "Put the work origin on any of the stock's nine anchors, type a position, or pick a hole centre in the viewport with snapping.",
  },
  {
    title: "Watch it cut first",
    body: "Toolpaths in a 2D and 3D viewport, rapids and cuts shown apart. The simulator plays the job back move by move: the bit, at its real shape, carves the stock as it goes. Scrub back and forth or jump between operations.",
  },
  {
    title: "G-code that runs",
    body: "Output for GRBL, grblHAL and FluidNC, with optional custom start, end and tool-change blocks per machine.",
  },
];
---

<section class="border-t border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">From drawing to G-code</h2>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        features.map((f) => (
          <div class="bg-bg p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold">{f.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted">{f.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-muted">
      Your tool library, machine profiles and projects are saved to your account, with undo, named
      versions and file export. Toolpaths are computed on your device, and the only personal data we
      keep is your email address.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
